<title>SINGAPORE: Ming Wah first-half net profit up 20 pct.</title>
<headline>Ming Wah first-half net profit up 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of US$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     4.81  vs   4.01</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    3.07  vs   2.60</p>
<p>    Turnover				17.73  vs  19.81</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    10.53  vs  10.40</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   1.68  vs   2.30</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   4.29  vs   4.28</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 4.81  vs   4.01</p>
<p>    Tax					 nil   vs   nil</p>
<p>NOTE - Ship-owning and chartering company Ming Wah Universal (Bermuda) Co Ltd is a unit of Hong Kong-listed China Merchants Hai Hong Holdings Co Ltd. The company was floated on the main board of the Stock Exchange of Singapore in June 1996.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
